[
  null,
  [
    "\nFor additional information on the equipment available, please read the >> Equipment Guide <<\n\nYou must carefully read the info below and check that you understand before booking.\n\nYou must have signed and returned an OFF-SITE PERMISSION FORM to take equipment off-site.\n\nBook at least 24 hours in advance wherever possible - the cut-off time for prebooking is 4:10pm the day before. \n\nBookings are not guaranteed due to limited equipment: it's a booking request not guarantee. \n\nPlease make sure to return equipment at the time and date you have filled out in the form; we use the DAY/MONTH/YEAR date system. \n\nEquipment is only allowed out for one night at a time, to be returned no later than 10:45am the following day, or over one weekend (Friday - Monday, returned no later than 10:45am). Please plan your filming accordingly.\n\nBookings are during term-time only, and are not permitted over half term or holidays.\n\nDo not leave equipment unattended or with another student. When signed out under your name, you are responsible for the equipment. \n\nWe operate a THREE STRIKE SYSTEM - Abandoning equipment, damaging equipment, no-shows and late returns without communication or good reason (e.g. being off sick) will result in a warning or strike.\n\nAny lost or damaged equipment must be reported as soon as it is noticed, or at the earliest convenience if it occurs while off-site - this includes by email, Teams message, or in-person either at the equipment hatch or in class.\n       \n=========================================================================\n\nPlease, email mediatech@longroad.ac.uk if you have any questions or problems, need to arrange an alternative pick-up time, or will be late returning equipment. You MUST contact the Media Technician if you will be late returning, as this may affect equipment availability for other students.\nTo book the Photography Studio, please contact the Media Technician to check for availability\n\nTo book a classroom please contact Student Services or visit Reception to find a vacant room\n\nTo use a Performing Arts room, please email the Performing Arts Technician, Amal: akurianjoseph@longroad.ac.uk",
